{title: This Is My Father's World}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
This [C]is my [G]Father's [C]world[C]
And [F]to my [C]listening [G]ears[G]
All [C]nature [Am]sings, and [G]round me [C]rings
The [F]music [G]of the [C]spheres[C]
This [C]is my [F]Father's [C]world[C]
I [F]rest me [G]in the [C]thought[C]
Of [G]rocks and [Am]trees, of [F]skies and [C]seas
His [F]hand the [G]wonders [C]wrought.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
This [C]is my [G]Father's [C]world[C]
The [F]birds their [C]carols [G]raise[G]
The [C]morning [Am]light, the [G]lily [C]white
De[F]clare their [G]Maker's [C]praise[C]
This [C]is my [F]Father's [C]world[C]
He [F]shines in [G]all that's [C]fair[C]
In the [G]rustling [Am]grass I [F]hear Him [C]pass
He [F]speaks to [G]me every[C]where.[C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
This [C]is my [G]Father's [C]world[C]
O [F]let me [C]ne'er for[G]get[G]
That [C]though the [F]wrong seems [G]oft so [C]strong
God [F]is the [G]Ruler [C]yet[C]
This [C]is my [F]Father's [C]world[C]
Why [F]should my [G]heart be [C]sad?[C]
The [G]Lord is [Am]King: let the [F]heavens [C]ring!
God [F]reigns; let [G]earth be [C]glad![C]
{end_of_verse}
